/-!
# Continuous tangent sections on Euclidean spheres and failure of projective cancellation

For a finite index type `ι` and a topological commutative `ℝ`-algebra `R`, let `S` be the unit
sphere `Metric.sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1` and `C(S, R)` the ring of continuous `R`-valued
functions on `S`. The coordinate functions `x ↦ xᵢ` define elements `TauCeti.sphereCoord R i` of
`C(S, R)` satisfying `∑ i, (sphereCoord R i) ^ 2 = 1` (see `TauCeti.Topology.Sphere.Coord`).

The submodule `TauCeti.tangentSections ι R` of `ι → C(S, R)` consists of those continuous fields
`v` orthogonal to the radial coordinate vector in the bilinear dot product,
`sphereCoord R ⬝ᵥ v = 0`. Equivalently, it is the range of the symmetric idempotent projection
matrix `TauCeti.sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R = 1 - x xᵀ`. Decomposing any ambient field into its
tangential and normal components yields an explicit `C(S, R)`-linear direct-sum splitting
`TauCeti.tangentSectionsSplitEquiv : (tangentSections ι R × C(S, R)) ≃ₗ[C(S, R)] (ι → C(S, R))`,
sending `(v, f)` to `v + f • x` with inverse `w ↦ (w - (x ⬝ᵥ w) • x, x ⬝ᵥ w)`. Consequently,
`tangentSections ι R` is finitely generated, projective, and stably free: for `ι = Fin (n + 1)` its
reduced class `TauCeti.FiniteProjectiveModules.classOf` in projective `K₀` vanishes, and its class
in `TauCeti.SplitK0` equals `n` times the class of the free rank-one module.

Whether `tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) ℝ` is actually free depends on the dimension `n` of the
sphere `Sⁿ`:

* For `S⁰` (`Fin 1`) it is the zero submodule, free of rank `0`.
* For `S¹` (`Fin 2`) it is free of rank `1` over every topological commutative `ℝ`-algebra `R`,
  generated by `(-x₁, x₀)` (`TauCeti.tangentSectionsCircleEquiv`).
* For every positive even `n` (`TauCeti.not_free_tangentSections_of_even`), and in particular for
  `S²` (`Fin 3`, `TauCeti.not_free_tangentSections_fin_three`), it is **not** free over
  `C(Sⁿ, ℝ)`:
  any free basis has `n` elements by rank, its first member defines a continuous tangent vector
  field on `Sⁿ`, and by the hairy ball theorem
  (`TauCeti.exists_eq_zero_of_continuous_of_inner_eq_zero`) that member vanishes at some point `x₀`,
  forcing the evaluations of `tangentSections` at `x₀` into an `(n - 1)`-dimensional subspace
  whereas the orthogonal complement of `x₀` has real dimension `n`.

On `S²`, this gives `P × R ≃ₗ[R] R³ ≃ₗ[R] R² × R` while `P` is not isomorphic to `R²`, witnessing
the failure of direct-sum cancellation for finitely generated projective modules over `C(S², ℝ)`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.tangentSections`: the submodule of `ι → C(S, R)` cut out by `sphereCoord R ⬝ᵥ v = 0`.
* `TauCeti.sphereTangentProjMatrix`: the symmetric idempotent matrix `1 - x xᵀ` projecting onto
  `tangentSections`.
* `TauCeti.tangentSectionsSplitEquiv`: the direct-sum isomorphism
  `(tangentSections ι R × C(S, R)) ≃ₗ[C(S, R)] (ι → C(S, R))`.
* `TauCeti.tangentSectionsCircleEquiv`: the rank-one trivialization
  `C(S¹, R) ≃ₗ[C(S¹, R)] tangentSections (Fin 2) R` via `(-x₁, x₀)`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.isIdempotentElem_sphereTangentProjMatrix`,
  `TauCeti.range_mulVecLin_sphereTangentProjMatrix`: `1 - x xᵀ` is idempotent with image
  `tangentSections`.
* `TauCeti.classOf_tangentSections`, `TauCeti.splitK0_of_tangentSections`: in `SplitK0` of finite
  projective modules over `C(Sⁿ, R)`, `[tangentSections] = n • [C(Sⁿ, R)]`.
* `TauCeti.not_free_tangentSections_of_even`: for positive even `n`,
  `tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) ℝ` is not free over `C(Sⁿ, ℝ)`.
* `TauCeti.not_free_tangentSections_fin_three`,
  `TauCeti.isEmpty_linearEquiv_tangentSections_fin_three_fin_two`:
  `tangentSections (Fin 3) ℝ` is not free over `C(S², ℝ)` and is not `C(S², ℝ)`-linearly
  isomorphic to `C(S², ℝ)²`.

## References

* R. G. Swan, *Vector bundles and projective modules*, Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. **105** (1962),
  264–277, Example 1.
* C. A. Weibel, *The K-book: An Introduction to Algebraic K-theory*, Graduate Studies in
  Mathematics 145, American Mathematical Society (2013), Chapter I, Example 1.2.2.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Matrix Metric
open scoped BigOperators InnerProductSpace

namespace TauCeti

section SubmoduleAndSplitting

variable (ι : Type*) [Fintype ι] (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [TopologicalSpace R]
  [IsTopologicalRing R] [Algebra ℝ R] [ContinuousSMul ℝ R]

/-- The continuous tangent-section module over `C(S, R)` on the unit sphere `S ⊂ ℝ^ι`: the kernel
of the `C(S, R)`-linear normal-component functional `v ↦ ∑ i, sphereCoord R i * v i`. -/
def tangentSections :
    Submodule C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)
      (ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)) :=
  LinearMap.ker (∑ i : ι, sphereCoord R i •
    (LinearMap.proj i : (ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)) →ₗ[
      C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)] C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)))

theorem tangentSections_def :
    tangentSections ι R =
      LinearMap.ker (∑ i : ι, sphereCoord R i •
        (LinearMap.proj i : (ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)) →ₗ[
          C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)] C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R))) :=
  (rfl)

variable {ι R}

/-- A continuous vector field lies in `tangentSections ι R` if and only if its bilinear dot product
with `sphereCoord R` vanishes. -/
@[simp]
theorem mem_tangentSections_iff {v : ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)} :
    v ∈ tangentSections ι R ↔ sphereCoord R ⬝ᵥ v = 0 := by
  simp [tangentSections_def, LinearMap.mem_ker, dotProduct, smul_eq_mul]

/-- Pointwise characterization of membership in `tangentSections ι R`. -/
theorem mem_tangentSections_iff_forall {v : ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)} :
    v ∈ tangentSections ι R ↔
      ∀ x : sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1,
        ∑ i : ι, algebraMap ℝ R ((x : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) i) * v i x = 0 := by
  rw [mem_tangentSections_iff, ContinuousMap.ext_iff]
  simp [dotProduct]

/-- Over `ℝ`, a continuous field lies in `tangentSections ι ℝ` if and only if its value at every
point `x` of the sphere is orthogonal to `x` in `EuclideanSpace ℝ ι`. -/
theorem mem_tangentSections_real_iff_inner
    {v : ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, ℝ)} :
    v ∈ tangentSections ι ℝ ↔
      ∀ x : sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1,
        ⟪WithLp.toLp 2 (fun i ↦ v i x), (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι)⟫_ℝ = 0 := by
  rw [mem_tangentSections_iff_forall]
  refine forall_congr' fun x ↦ ?_
  rw [real_inner_comm, EuclideanSpace.inner_eq_star_dotProduct, star_trivial, dotProduct]
  simp [mul_comm]

section ProjectionMatrix

variable (ι R) [DecidableEq ι]

/-- The orthogonal-projection matrix `p(x) = 1 - x xᵀ` in `M_ι(C(S, R))` cutting out
`tangentSections ι R`. -/
def sphereTangentProjMatrix : Matrix ι ι C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R) :=
  1 - vecMulVec (sphereCoord R) (sphereCoord R)

theorem sphereTangentProjMatrix_def :
    sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R = 1 - vecMulVec (sphereCoord R) (sphereCoord R) :=
  (rfl)

variable {ι R}

theorem sphereTangentProjMatrix_apply (i j : ι) :
    sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R i j =
      (1 : Matrix ι ι C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)) i j -
        sphereCoord R i * sphereCoord R j :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem transpose_sphereTangentProjMatrix :
    (sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R)ᵀ = sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R := by
  simp [sphereTangentProjMatrix_def]

theorem isSymm_sphereTangentProjMatrix : (sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R).IsSymm :=
  transpose_sphereTangentProjMatrix

/-- Entrywise application of a continuous `ℝ`-algebra homomorphism carries
`sphereTangentProjMatrix` over `R` to `sphereTangentProjMatrix` over `S`. -/
@[simp]
theorem map_sphereTangentProjMatrix {S : Type*} [CommRing S] [TopologicalSpace S]
    [IsTopologicalRing S] [Algebra ℝ S] [ContinuousSMul ℝ S] (φ : R →ₐ[ℝ] S) (hφ : Continuous φ) :
    (sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R).map ((φ : R →+* S).compLeftContinuous _ hφ) =
      sphereTangentProjMatrix ι S := by
  rw [sphereTangentProjMatrix_def, sphereTangentProjMatrix_def, Matrix.map_sub _ (map_sub _),
    Matrix.map_one _ (map_zero _) (map_one _)]
  refine congrArg (1 - ·) (Matrix.ext fun i j ↦ ?_)
  simp [vecMulVec_apply]

theorem vecMul_sphereTangentProjMatrix (v : ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)) :
    v ᵥ* sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R = v - (sphereCoord R ⬝ᵥ v) • sphereCoord R := by
  rw [sphereTangentProjMatrix_def, vecMul_sub, vecMul_one, vecMul_vecMulVec, dotProduct_comm]

theorem sphereTangentProjMatrix_mulVec (v : ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)) :
    sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R *ᵥ v = v - (sphereCoord R ⬝ᵥ v) • sphereCoord R := by
  rw [← transpose_sphereTangentProjMatrix, mulVec_transpose, vecMul_sphereTangentProjMatrix]

@[simp]
theorem sphereTangentProjMatrix_mulVec_sphereCoord :
    sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R *ᵥ sphereCoord R = 0 := by
  rw [sphereTangentProjMatrix_mulVec, dotProduct_sphereCoord_self, one_smul, sub_self]

/-- On the unit sphere, `1 - x xᵀ` is an idempotent matrix:
`(1 - x xᵀ)² = 1 - 2 x xᵀ + x (xᵀ x) xᵀ = 1 - x xᵀ`. -/
theorem isIdempotentElem_sphereTangentProjMatrix :
    IsIdempotentElem (sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R) := by
  simpa only [IsIdempotentElem, sphereTangentProjMatrix_def, sub_zero, one_smul, zero_smul,
    add_zero] using
    one_sub_vecMulVec_mul_self (0 : C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R))
      (u := sphereCoord R) (v := sphereCoord R) (by rw [dotProduct_sphereCoord_self, zero_add])

theorem sphereTangentProjMatrix_mulVec_eq_self_iff
    {v : ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)} :
    sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R *ᵥ v = v ↔ v ∈ tangentSections ι R := by
  rw [sphereTangentProjMatrix_mulVec, sub_eq_self, mem_tangentSections_iff]
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ?_, fun h ↦ by rw [h, zero_smul]⟩
  have hdot := congrArg (sphereCoord R ⬝ᵥ ·) h
  simpa only [dotProduct_smul, dotProduct_sphereCoord_self, smul_eq_mul, mul_one,
    dotProduct_zero] using hdot

/-- The image of `1 - x xᵀ` acting on column vectors is `tangentSections ι R`. -/
theorem range_mulVecLin_sphereTangentProjMatrix :
    LinearMap.range (sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R).mulVecLin = tangentSections ι R := by
  ext v
  rw [← sphereTangentProjMatrix_mulVec_eq_self_iff]
  refine ⟨?_, fun h ↦ ⟨v, h⟩⟩
  rintro ⟨u, rfl⟩
  simp only [mulVecLin_apply, mulVec_mulVec, isIdempotentElem_sphereTangentProjMatrix.eq]

/-- The image of `1 - x xᵀ` acting on row vectors is also `tangentSections ι R`. -/
theorem range_vecMulLinear_sphereTangentProjMatrix :
    LinearMap.range (sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R).vecMulLinear = tangentSections ι R := by
  rw [← range_mulVecLin_sphereTangentProjMatrix]
  ext v
  simp only [LinearMap.mem_range, vecMulLinear_apply, mulVecLin_apply,
    vecMul_sphereTangentProjMatrix, sphereTangentProjMatrix_mulVec]

/-- The trace of `1 - x xᵀ` on a nonempty index set `ι` is `card ι - 1`. -/
theorem trace_sphereTangentProjMatrix [Nonempty ι] :
    Matrix.trace (sphereTangentProjMatrix ι R) = (Fintype.card ι - 1 : ℕ) := by
  have hcard : 1 ≤ Fintype.card ι := Fintype.card_pos
  rw [sphereTangentProjMatrix_def, trace_sub, trace_one, trace, diag_vecMulVec]
  simp only [Pi.mul_apply, ← sq, sum_sphereCoord_sq, Nat.cast_sub hcard, Nat.cast_one]

end ProjectionMatrix

variable (ι R) in
/-- Tangential-normal decomposition on the unit sphere: `tangentSections ι R ⊕ C(S, R) ≃ C(S, R)^ι`,
sending `(v, f)` to `v + f • sphereCoord R` with inverse
`w ↦ (w - (sphereCoord R ⬝ᵥ w) • sphereCoord R, sphereCoord R ⬝ᵥ w)`. -/
def tangentSectionsSplitEquiv :
    (tangentSections ι R × C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)) ≃ₗ[
      C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)]
      (ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)) where
  toFun p := (p.1 : ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)) + p.2 • sphereCoord R
  invFun w :=
    (⟨w - (sphereCoord R ⬝ᵥ w) • sphereCoord R, by
        rw [mem_tangentSections_iff, dotProduct_sub, dotProduct_smul, dotProduct_sphereCoord_self,
          smul_eq_mul, mul_one, sub_self]⟩,
      sphereCoord R ⬝ᵥ w)
  map_add' p q := by
    refine funext fun i ↦ ?_
    simp only [Prod.fst_add, Submodule.coe_add, Prod.snd_add, Pi.add_apply, Pi.smul_apply,
      smul_eq_mul]
    ring
  map_smul' c p := by
    ext i x
    simp [mul_add, mul_assoc]
  left_inv p := by
    have hp : sphereCoord R ⬝ᵥ (p.1 : ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)) = 0 :=
      mem_tangentSections_iff.mp p.1.property
    ext1
    · ext i
      simp [dotProduct_add, hp, dotProduct_smul, dotProduct_sphereCoord_self]
    · simp [dotProduct_add, hp, dotProduct_smul, dotProduct_sphereCoord_self]
  right_inv w := by
    ext i x
    simp

@[simp]
theorem tangentSectionsSplitEquiv_apply
    (p : tangentSections ι R × C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)) :
    tangentSectionsSplitEquiv ι R p =
      (p.1 : ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)) + p.2 • sphereCoord R :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem coe_fst_tangentSectionsSplitEquiv_symm_apply
    (w : ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)) :
    ((tangentSectionsSplitEquiv ι R).symm w).1.val =
      w - (sphereCoord R ⬝ᵥ w) • sphereCoord R :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem snd_tangentSectionsSplitEquiv_symm_apply
    (w : ι → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R)) :
    ((tangentSectionsSplitEquiv ι R).symm w).2 = sphereCoord R ⬝ᵥ w :=
  (rfl)

instance : Module.Finite C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R) (tangentSections ι R) :=
  Module.Finite.of_surjective
    ((LinearMap.fst _ _ _).comp (tangentSectionsSplitEquiv ι R).symm.toLinearMap)
    (Prod.fst_surjective.comp (tangentSectionsSplitEquiv ι R).symm.surjective)

instance : Module.Projective C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ ι) 1, R) (tangentSections ι R) :=
  Module.Projective.of_split (tangentSections ι R).subtype
    ((LinearMap.fst _ _ _).comp (tangentSectionsSplitEquiv ι R).symm.toLinearMap) <| by
      ext ⟨v, hv⟩
      have h0 : sphereCoord R ⬝ᵥ v = 0 := mem_tangentSections_iff.mp hv
      simp [h0]

/-- In projective `K₀` of `C(Sⁿ, R)`, the reduced class `[tangentSections] - n[C(Sⁿ, R)]`
vanishes. -/
@[simp]
theorem classOf_tangentSections (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R]
    [TopologicalSpace R] [IsTopologicalRing R] [Algebra ℝ R] [ContinuousSMul ℝ R] :
    FiniteProjectiveModules.classOf
        C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1, R)
        (tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) R) n = 0 := by
  let A := C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1, R)
  have h1 : FiniteProjectiveModules.classOf A A 1 = 0 := by
    rw [FiniteProjectiveModules.classOf_congr (LinearEquiv.funUnique (Fin 1) A A).symm 1]
    exact FiniteProjectiveModules.classOf_free A 1
  have hsum :
      FiniteProjectiveModules.classOf A (tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) R) n +
        FiniteProjectiveModules.classOf A A 1 = 0 := by
    rw [← FiniteProjectiveModules.classOf_prod n 1,
      FiniteProjectiveModules.classOf_congr (tangentSectionsSplitEquiv (Fin (n + 1)) R) (n + 1)]
    exact FiniteProjectiveModules.classOf_free A (n + 1)
  rwa [h1, add_zero] at hsum

/-- In `SplitK0` of finitely generated projective `C(Sⁿ, R)`-modules, the class of
`tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) R` is `n` times the class of `C(Sⁿ, R)`. -/
theorem splitK0_of_tangentSections.{u} (n : ℕ) (R : Type u) [CommRing R]
    [TopologicalSpace R] [IsTopologicalRing R] [Algebra ℝ R] [ContinuousSMul ℝ R] :
    SplitK0.of.{u}
        (⟨ModuleCat.of C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1, R)
            (tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) R),
          finiteProjectiveModules_iff.2 ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩⟩ :
          (finiteProjectiveModules
            C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1, R)).FullSubcategory) =
      n • SplitK0.of.{u}
        (⟨ModuleCat.of C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1, R)
            C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1, R),
          finiteProjectiveModules_iff.2 ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩⟩ :
          (finiteProjectiveModules
            C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1, R)).FullSubcategory) := by
  rw [← sub_eq_zero, ← FiniteProjectiveModules.classOf_def]
  exact classOf_tangentSections n R

/-- Whenever `tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) R` is free over `C(Sⁿ, R)` with `R` nontrivial, its
`C(Sⁿ, R)`-rank is `n`. -/
theorem finrank_tangentSections (n : ℕ) (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Nontrivial R]
    [TopologicalSpace R] [IsTopologicalRing R] [Algebra ℝ R] [ContinuousSMul ℝ R]
    [Module.Free C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1, R)
      (tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) R)] :
    Module.finrank C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1, R)
      (tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) R) = n := by
  let S := sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1
  let A := C(S, R)
  let P := tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) R
  have hprod : Module.finrank A P + 1 = n + 1 := by
    calc
      Module.finrank A P + 1 = Module.finrank A P + Module.finrank A A := by
        rw [Module.finrank_self]
      _ = Module.finrank A (P × A) := (Module.finrank_prod (R := A) (M := P) (M' := A)).symm
      _ = Module.finrank A (Fin (n + 1) → A) :=
        LinearEquiv.finrank_eq (tangentSectionsSplitEquiv (Fin (n + 1)) R)
      _ = n + 1 := by simp
  exact Nat.add_right_cancel hprod

end SubmoduleAndSplitting

section LowDimensions

variable (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [TopologicalSpace R] [IsTopologicalRing R]
  [Algebra ℝ R] [ContinuousSMul ℝ R]

/-- On `S⁰ ⊂ ℝ¹`, the continuous tangent-section submodule `tangentSections (Fin 1) R` is
trivial. -/
@[simp]
theorem tangentSections_fin_one_eq_bot : tangentSections (Fin 1) R = ⊥ := by
  ext v
  rw [Submodule.mem_bot, mem_tangentSections_iff]
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ funext fun i ↦ ?_, fun h ↦ by simp [h]⟩
  fin_cases i
  have h1 : sphereCoord R (0 : Fin 1) * sphereCoord R (0 : Fin 1) = 1 := by
    simpa [dotProduct] using dotProduct_sphereCoord_self (R := R) (ι := Fin 1)
  have hv : sphereCoord R (0 : Fin 1) * v 0 = 0 := by simpa [dotProduct] using h
  calc
    v 0 = 1 * v 0 := (one_mul _).symm
    _ = (sphereCoord R (0 : Fin 1) * sphereCoord R (0 : Fin 1)) * v 0 := by rw [h1]
    _ = sphereCoord R (0 : Fin 1) * (sphereCoord R (0 : Fin 1) * v 0) := mul_assoc _ _ _
    _ = 0 := by rw [hv, mul_zero]

instance : Module.Free C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)) 1, R)
    (tangentSections (Fin 1) R) := by
  have : Subsingleton (tangentSections (Fin 1) R) :=
    ⟨fun ⟨v, hv⟩ ⟨w, hw⟩ ↦ by
      rw [tangentSections_fin_one_eq_bot R, Submodule.mem_bot] at hv hw
      exact Subtype.ext (hv.trans hw.symm)⟩
  exact Module.Free.of_equiv (LinearEquiv.ofSubsingleton
    (Fin 0 → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)) 1, R)) (tangentSections (Fin 1) R))

private theorem sphereCoord_fin_two_sq_add_sq :
    sphereCoord R (0 : Fin 2) ^ 2 + sphereCoord R (1 : Fin 2) ^ 2 = 1 := by
  simpa only [Fin.sum_univ_two] using sum_sphereCoord_sq (R := R) (ι := Fin 2)

/-- On `S¹ ⊂ ℝ²`, `tangentSections (Fin 2) R` is free of rank one over `C(S¹, R)`, generated by the
nowhere-vanishing tangent field `(-x₁, x₀)`. -/
def tangentSectionsCircleEquiv :
    C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) 1, R) ≃ₗ[
      C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) 1, R)]
      tangentSections (Fin 2) R where
  toFun f :=
    ⟨![-f * sphereCoord R 1, f * sphereCoord R 0], by
      rw [mem_tangentSections_iff, dotProduct, Fin.sum_univ_two]
      simp only [cons_val_zero, cons_val_one]
      ring⟩
  invFun v := -sphereCoord R 1 * (v : Fin 2 → _) 0 + sphereCoord R 0 * (v : Fin 2 → _) 1
  map_add' f g := by
    refine Subtype.ext (funext fun i ↦ ?_)
    fin_cases i <;>
      simp only [Fin.zero_eta, Fin.mk_one, Submodule.coe_add, Pi.add_apply, cons_val_zero,
        cons_val_one] <;>
      ring
  map_smul' c f := by
    refine Subtype.ext (funext fun i ↦ ?_)
    fin_cases i <;>
      simp only [Fin.zero_eta, Fin.mk_one, RingHom.id_apply, SetLike.val_smul, Pi.smul_apply,
        smul_eq_mul, cons_val_zero, cons_val_one] <;>
      ring
  left_inv f := by
    simp only [cons_val_zero, cons_val_one]
    linear_combination f * sphereCoord_fin_two_sq_add_sq R
  right_inv v := by
    have hv : sphereCoord R (0 : Fin 2) * v.val 0 + sphereCoord R (1 : Fin 2) * v.val 1 = 0 := by
      simpa [dotProduct, Fin.sum_univ_two] using mem_tangentSections_iff.mp v.property
    refine Subtype.ext (funext fun i ↦ ?_)
    fin_cases i
    · simp only [Fin.zero_eta, cons_val_zero]
      linear_combination v.val 0 * sphereCoord_fin_two_sq_add_sq R - sphereCoord R (0 : Fin 2) * hv
    · simp only [Fin.mk_one, cons_val_one, cons_val_zero]
      linear_combination v.val 1 * sphereCoord_fin_two_sq_add_sq R - sphereCoord R (1 : Fin 2) * hv

@[simp]
theorem coe_tangentSectionsCircleEquiv_apply
    (f : C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) 1, R)) :
    (tangentSectionsCircleEquiv R f : Fin 2 → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) 1, R)) =
      ![-f * sphereCoord R 1, f * sphereCoord R 0] :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem tangentSectionsCircleEquiv_symm_apply (v : tangentSections (Fin 2) R) :
    (tangentSectionsCircleEquiv R).symm v =
      -sphereCoord R 1 * v.val 0 + sphereCoord R 0 * v.val 1 :=
  (rfl)

instance : Module.Free C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) 1, R)
    (tangentSections (Fin 2) R) :=
  Module.Free.of_equiv (tangentSectionsCircleEquiv R)

end LowDimensions

section NonFreeEvenSphere

/-- Pointwise evaluation of a tangent-section field at a point `x₀` of the unit sphere as an
`ℝ`-linear map into `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))`. -/
private def evalTangentAt {n : ℕ} (x₀ : sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1) :
    tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) ℝ →ₗ[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1)) where
  toFun v := WithLp.toLp 2 fun j ↦ v.val j x₀
  map_add' v w := by ext j; rfl
  map_smul' r v := by ext j; rfl

@[simp]
private theorem evalTangentAt_apply {n : ℕ}
    (x₀ : sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1)
    (v : tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) ℝ) :
    evalTangentAt x₀ v = WithLp.toLp 2 fun j ↦ v.val j x₀ :=
  (rfl)

private theorem evalTangentAt_smul_fun {n : ℕ}
    (x₀ : sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1)
    (c : C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1, ℝ))
    (v : tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) ℝ) :
    evalTangentAt x₀ (c • v) = c x₀ • evalTangentAt x₀ v := by
  ext j
  rfl

/-- Evaluating `tangentSections` at any point `x₀ ∈ Sⁿ` covers the entire orthogonal complement of
`x₀` in `ℝⁿ⁺¹`: for `y ⊥ x₀`, the tangential projection of the constant field `y` evaluates at `x₀`
to `y`. -/
private theorem orthogonal_le_range_evalTangentAt {n : ℕ}
    (x₀ : sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1) :
    (ℝ ∙ (x₀ : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))))ᗮ ≤ LinearMap.range (evalTangentAt x₀) := by
  intro y hy
  have hxy : ⟪(x₀ : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))), y⟫_ℝ = 0 :=
    Submodule.inner_right_of_mem_orthogonal (Submodule.mem_span_singleton_self _) hy
  have hdot : (sphereCoord ℝ ⬝ᵥ fun j ↦ ContinuousMap.const _ (y j)) x₀ = 0 := by
    rw [EuclideanSpace.inner_eq_star_dotProduct, star_trivial, dotProduct] at hxy
    simpa [dotProduct, mul_comm] using hxy
  refine ⟨((tangentSectionsSplitEquiv (Fin (n + 1)) ℝ).symm
    (fun j ↦ ContinuousMap.const _ (y j))).1, ?_⟩
  ext j
  simp [hdot]

/-- No `C(S^{k+1}, ℝ)`-basis of `tangentSections (Fin (k + 2)) ℝ` of size `k + 1` exists when
`k + 1` is even: the `0`-th basis field vanishes at some `x₀ ∈ S^{k+1}` by the hairy ball theorem,
forcing the evaluations of all tangent sections at `x₀` into the span of the remaining `k` vectors
whereas `(ℝ ∙ x₀)ᗮ` has dimension `k + 1`. -/
private theorem not_basis_tangentSections_of_even {k : ℕ} (hk : Even (k + 1))
    (b : Module.Basis (Fin (k + 1))
      C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (k + 2))) 1, ℝ)
      (tangentSections (Fin (k + 2)) ℝ)) : False := by
  have : Fact (Module.finrank ℝ (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (k + 2))) = (k + 1) + 1) :=
    ⟨finrank_euclideanSpace_fin⟩
  have hcont : Continuous fun x : sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (k + 2))) 1 ↦
      WithLp.toLp 2 fun j ↦ (b 0).val j x :=
    (PiLp.continuous_toLp 2 _).comp (continuous_pi fun j ↦ ((b 0).val j).continuous)
  have hinner : ∀ x : sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (k + 2))) 1,
      ⟪WithLp.toLp 2 (fun j ↦ (b 0).val j x), (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ _)⟫_ℝ = 0 :=
    mem_tangentSections_real_iff_inner.mp (b 0).property
  obtain ⟨x₀, hx₀⟩ := exists_eq_zero_of_continuous_of_inner_eq_zero (n := k + 1) hk hcont hinner
  have hx₀' : evalTangentAt x₀ (b 0) = 0 := by rw [evalTangentAt_apply]; exact hx₀
  have hrange_le : LinearMap.range (evalTangentAt x₀) ≤
      Submodule.span ℝ (Set.range fun j : Fin k ↦ evalTangentAt x₀ (b j.succ)) := by
    rintro _ ⟨v, rfl⟩
    have hev : evalTangentAt x₀ v =
        ∑ j : Fin k, (b.repr v j.succ x₀) • evalTangentAt x₀ (b j.succ) := by
      conv_lhs => rw [← b.sum_repr v]
      rw [map_sum, Fin.sum_univ_succ, evalTangentAt_smul_fun, hx₀', smul_zero, zero_add]
      exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ ↦ evalTangentAt_smul_fun x₀ _ _
    rw [hev]
    exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun j _ ↦ Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨j, rfl⟩)
  have hle₁ : k + 1 ≤ Module.finrank ℝ (LinearMap.range (evalTangentAt x₀)) :=
    (Submodule.finrank_orthogonal_span_singleton (ne_zero_of_mem_unit_sphere x₀)).symm.le.trans
      (Submodule.finrank_mono (orthogonal_le_range_evalTangentAt x₀))
  have hle₂ : Module.finrank ℝ (LinearMap.range (evalTangentAt x₀)) ≤ k :=
    (Submodule.finrank_mono hrange_le).trans <|
      (finrank_range_le_card fun j : Fin k ↦ evalTangentAt x₀ (b j.succ)).trans_eq
        (Fintype.card_fin k)
  omega

/-- For every positive even `n`, the continuous tangent-section module
`tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) ℝ` is not free over `C(Sⁿ, ℝ)`. -/
theorem not_free_tangentSections_of_even {n : ℕ} (hn : Even n) (hn0 : n ≠ 0) :
    ¬ Module.Free C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n + 1))) 1, ℝ)
        (tangentSections (Fin (n + 1)) ℝ) := by
  intro hfree
  obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_succ_of_ne_zero hn0
  have hcard : Fintype.card
      (Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex
        C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (k + 2))) 1, ℝ)
        (tangentSections (Fin (k + 2)) ℝ)) = k + 1 := by
    rw [← Module.finrank_eq_card_chooseBasisIndex]
    exact finrank_tangentSections (k + 1) ℝ
  exact not_basis_tangentSections_of_even hn
    ((Module.Free.chooseBasis _ _).reindex (Fintype.equivFinOfCardEq hcard))

/-- The continuous tangent-section module on the two-sphere `S² ⊂ ℝ³` is not free over
`C(S², ℝ)` (continuous-function counterpart of Weibel, *The K-book*, Chapter I, Example 1.2.2; see
also Swan, 1962, Example 1). -/
theorem not_free_tangentSections_fin_three :
    ¬ Module.Free C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 3)) 1, ℝ) (tangentSections (Fin 3) ℝ) :=
  not_free_tangentSections_of_even (n := 2) even_two two_ne_zero

/-- There is no `C(S², ℝ)`-linear isomorphism between `tangentSections (Fin 3) ℝ` and
`C(S², ℝ)²`. -/
theorem isEmpty_linearEquiv_tangentSections_fin_three_fin_two :
    IsEmpty (tangentSections (Fin 3) ℝ ≃ₗ[C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 3)) 1, ℝ)]
      (Fin 2 → C(sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 3)) 1, ℝ))) :=
  ⟨fun e ↦ not_free_tangentSections_fin_three (Module.Free.of_equiv e.symm)⟩

end NonFreeEvenSphere

end TauCeti
